      "fact": "The state of Georgia is filled with a very dark red color, appearing to be the darkest shade on the entire map."
    },
    {
      "location": "Rhode Island (RI) is located in the northeastern region of the map.",
      "fact": "The state of Rhode Island is filled with a medium red color, which is lighter than the shade used for Georgia."
    },
    {
      "location": "Delaware (DE) is located on the east coast, north of Maryland.",
      "fact": "The state of Delaware is filled with a light yellow-orange color, indicating a low value on the scale."
    },
    {
      "location": "New Mexico (NM), Wyoming (WY), Oklahoma (OK), and South Dakota (SD) are located in the western and central regions.",
      "fact": "Several other states share the same dark red coloration as Georgia, indicating similarly low prevalence values."
    },
    {
      "location": "States such as Idaho (ID), New York (NY), and West Virginia (WV) are located across the western, northeastern, and mid-Atlantic regions.",
      "fact": "These states are colored in very light yellow, representing the highest values on the provided scale."
    }
  ],
  "printed_facts": [
